							            <div id="main-content" class="main-container clearfix">
							              
                            <!-- OC Layout Element Conent Template -->
							              <!--normalTemplateStart--><div class="grid">
    <div class="col-xs-12 col-m-8">
        <h1 class='oc-page-title '>2026 General Election</h1>
        
        <p style="text-align: left;">Mesa will hold a <strong>General Election on November 3, 2026</strong> for a District 5 Councilmember runoff, and consideration of four ballot measures. Details about the District 5 candidates and the ballot questions are shown below.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><a href="https://library.municode.com/az/mesa/munidocs/munidocs?nodeId=9297722b70dd2" target="_blank"><strong>Resolution No. 12537 - Call of Election</strong></a>&nbsp;(<strong><a title="Spanish version of Resolution 12537" href="/files/assets/public/v/1/government/cityclerk/2026election/res-12537.pdf" target="_self" class=" document ext-pdf"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>En Espa&ntilde;ol<span class="file-info">(PDF,&nbsp;99KB)</span></a></strong>)</p>
<h2>General Key Election Dates</h2>
<table align="center" class="" style="width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td headers="table_heading_0" style="width: 25%; background-color: rgb(15,36,62);" class=""><strong>&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(255,255,255);">September 19</span></strong></td>
<td headers="table_heading_1" style="width: 75%; border-color: rgb(216,216,216); border-width: 1px; border-style: solid;" class="">&nbsp;Military and overseas ballots mailed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="" style="width: 25%; background-color: rgb(23,54,93);" headers="table_heading_0"><strong>&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(255,255,255);">October 5</span></strong></td>
<td class="" style="width: 75%; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(216,216,216);" headers="table_heading_1">&nbsp;Last day to register to vote in the General Election</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="" style="width: 25%; background-color: rgb(54,96,146);" headers="table_heading_0"><strong>&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(255,255,255);">October 7</span></strong></td>
<td class="" style="width: 75%; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(216,216,216);" headers="table_heading_1">&nbsp;Ballots mailed and early voting begins</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 25%; background-color: rgb(0,112,192);" headers="table_heading_0">&nbsp;<strong><span style="color: rgb(255,255,255);">October 23</span></strong></td>
<td class="" style="width: 75%; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(216,216,216);" headers="table_heading_1">&nbsp;Last day to request ballot by mail</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="" style="width: 25%; background-color: rgb(84,141,212);" headers="table_heading_0">&nbsp;<strong><span style="color: rgb(255,255,255);">October 27</span></strong></td>
<td class="" style="width: 75%; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(216,216,216);" headers="table_heading_1">&nbsp;Last day to mail back your ballot</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="" style="width: 25%; background-color: rgb(192,0,0);" headers="table_heading_0"><strong>&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(255,255,255);">November 3</span></strong></td>
<td class="" style="width: 75%; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(216,216,216);" headers="table_heading_1">&nbsp;Election Day!</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Voter and Ballot Information</h2>
<p>Sign in to the voter dashboard to find your personalized election information. Review your <strong>voter registration information</strong>, <strong>sample ballot</strong>, <strong>voting location information</strong> and your <strong>ballot status</strong>. Everything you need to #BeBallotReady can be found on the dashboard.</p>
<div data-layout="3" data-title-level="3" class="featured-links featured-links-option-3">
<div class="featured-links-body clearfix">
<ul class="clearfix">
<li><a class="featured-link" href="https://elections.maricopa.gov/voting/voter-dashboard-login" target="_blank">Voter Dashboard</a></li>
<li><a class="featured-link" href="https://elections.maricopa.gov/voting/voter-dashboard-login" target="_blank">Sample Ballot</a></li>
<li><a class="featured-link" href="https://www.mesaaz.gov/Government/City-Clerk/Elections/GeneralElection#docaccess-3129882b55997f5e6fbee2cd7dfed3fe" target="_blank">Publicity Pamphlet</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<h2>Mesa Ballot Measures for the General Election</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/DRxNGNv2fGI?si=YvN87ZHzpVMx-tzk" title="General Election ballot questions" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></p>
<div data-type="0" data-title-level="3" class="oc-wysiwyg-container">
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h3>Question 1. General Obligation Bond: Enhance Public Safety</h3>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p><strong><a href="https://library.municode.com/az/mesa/munidocs/munidocs?nodeId=92977231d0c79" target="_blank">Resolution No. 12538</a>&nbsp;(</strong><a title="Spanish version of Resolution 12538" href="/files/assets/public/v/1/government/cityclerk/2026election/res-12538.pdf" target="_self" class="document ext-pdf"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>En Espa&ntilde;ol<span class="file-info">(PDF,&nbsp;205KB)</span></a>)</p>
<p>Shall Mesa be authorized to issue and sell $150,000,000 of general obligation bonds to provide funding to support fire and medical, police, and public safety improvements, facilities, and communication systems, associated equipment, apparatuses, and technology, municipal improvements that support community and public safety, and acquisition of land for such purposes?</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.mesaaz.gov/Government/City-Clerk/Elections/GeneralElection/2026Bond">2026 General Obligation Bond Proposal details</a></strong></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h3>Question 2. General Obligation Bond: Enhance Transportation Improvements for Safer and Less Congested Streets</h3>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p><strong><a href="https://library.municode.com/az/mesa/munidocs/munidocs?nodeId=92977231d0c79" target="_blank">Resolution No. 12538</a>&nbsp;(</strong><a title="Spanish version of Resolution 12538" href="/files/assets/public/v/1/government/cityclerk/2026election/res-12538.pdf" target="_self" class="document ext-pdf"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>En Espa&ntilde;ol<span class="file-info">(PDF,&nbsp;205KB)</span></a>)</p>
<p>Shall Mesa be authorized to issue and sell $135,000,000 of general obligation bonds to provide funding to support safer and less congested streets, including for arterial street improvements, pavement reconstruction, street improvements, streetlights, traffic signals, communication infrastructure, shared use paths, associated improvements, and the acquisition of land for such purposes?</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.mesaaz.gov/Government/City-Clerk/Elections/GeneralElection/2026Bond">2026 General Obligation Bond Proposal details</a></strong></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h3>Question 3. Charter Amendment: Section 209(A) Relating to Council Meeting Procedures and Public Notice</h3>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p><strong><a href="https://library.municode.com/az/mesa/munidocs/munidocs?nodeId=929766c9ffbfa" target="_blank">Ordinance No. 6017</a>&nbsp;(</strong><a title="Spanish version of Ordinance 6017" href="/files/assets/public/v/1/government/cityclerk/2026election/ordinance-6017.pdf" target="_self" class="document ext-pdf"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>En Espa&ntilde;ol<span class="file-info">(PDF,&nbsp;141KB)</span></a>)</p>
<p>To conform with state law, shall Mesa City Charter Section 209(A) relating to Council meetings be amended to require that the procedures for fixing the time and place of regular meetings and giving public notice of meetings, and the purposes for executive sessions be in accordance with state law?</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h3>Question 4. Charter Amendment: Section 211 Relating to Ordinance Posting and Publication</h3>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p><strong><a href="https://library.municode.com/az/mesa/munidocs/munidocs?nodeId=929766a6dbf33" target="_blank">Ordinance No. 6016</a>&nbsp;(</strong><a title="Spanish version of Ordinance 6016" href="/files/assets/public/v/1/government/cityclerk/2026election/ordinance-6016.pdf" target="_self" class="document ext-pdf"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>En Espa&ntilde;ol<span class="file-info">(PDF,&nbsp;164KB)</span></a>)</p>
<p>To conform with state law modernization efforts, shall Mesa City Charter Section 211 relating to ordinances be amended to require ordinances to be posted on the City&rsquo;s website, posted at one physical location in Mesa, and published in accordance with state law?</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h3>District 5 Councilmember Runoff</h3>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p><strong>For Residents of District 5<br /></strong>The following candidates will appear on your ballot in the City Council runoff election:</p>
<p><strong>Alicia Goforth</strong><br />
<a href="mailto:goforthformesa@gmail.com">goforthformesa@gmail.com</a><br />
<a href="https://goforthformesa.com/" target="_blank">Goforthformesa.com</a></p>
<p><strong>Aleks Vranicic</strong><br />
<a href="mailto:aleks@aleksformesa.com">aleks@aleksformesa.com</a><br />
<a href="https://www.aleksformesa.com/" target="_blank">aleksformesa.com</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h3>Pro/Con Argument Form</h3>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<h4>Deadline</h4>
<ul>
<li>Pro/Con arguments for the publicity pamphlet must be filed with the City Clerk's Office at <strong>20 East Main Street, Suite 150, Mesa, Arizona 85201</strong> no later than <strong>6:00 p.m. on August 5, 2026.</strong></li>
</ul>
<h4>Pro/Con Argument Requirements</h4>
<ul>
<li>Arguments may not exceed 300 words.</li>
<li>Each argument must include a sworn statement and the original signature(s) of every person sponsoring the argument.</li>
<li>Arguments for or against the authorization of one or more bond questions that are submitted by an individual, and not on behalf of an organization, political committee, or other group, must include a sworn, <strong><a title="Notarized statement" href="/files/assets/public/v/1/government/cityclerk/2026election/notarial-certificate-for-bond-arguments.pdf" target="_self" class="document ext-pdf"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>notarized statement<span class="file-info">(PDF,&nbsp;94KB)</span></a></strong>.</li>
<li>The address and telephone number of each signer must be included with the submission; however, this information will not be published in the publicity pamphlet.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Filing Fee and Payment Information</h4>
<ul>
<li>A $250 filing fee is required for each argument submitted. This fee helps offset a portion of the cost of printing and distributing the publicity pamphlet.</li>
<li>If payment will be made by credit card, arrangements must be made in advance by contacting the City Clerk's Office at <strong><a href="tel:4806442099">480-644-2099</a></strong>.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Pro/Con Argument Submission</h4>
<ul type="disc">
<li>All arguments must first be submitted using the online <strong><a href="https://us.openforms.com/Form/6d819e0e-35cf-4bb4-a8f3-3f227792e9a9" target="_blank">Argument Submission Form</a></strong>.</li>
<li>Once the electronic form is submitted, a PDF Statement form will be emailed to you to print and sign.</li>
<li>Arguments are <strong>not considered officially filed</strong> until the following have been received by the City Clerk's Office prior to the filing deadline:</li>
<li style="list-style: none; display: inline">
<ul type="circle">
<li>The original signed argument and sworn statement with original signatures; and</li>
<li>The required $250 filing fee.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4>Filing Process</h4>
<ul>
<li>Arguments are printed in the publicity pamphlet in the order they are officially filed with the City Clerk's Office.</li>
<li>To submit the original signed argument, please contact the City Clerk's Office at <strong><a href="tel:4806442099">480-644-2099</a></strong> to schedule an appointment prior to the filing deadline.</li>
</ul>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://us.openforms.com/Form/6d819e0e-35cf-4bb4-a8f3-3f227792e9a9" target="_blank" class="styled-button">Argument Submission Form</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>


      
        
    </div>
    
